course: dictionary
lesson: 10143
title: Thrive: growing and doing well
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Thrive is a verb, a word for an action. A plant thrives when it gets light, water and good soil: it grows strong and healthy. A child can thrive too when she is happy and doing well.
explain: Look at the sentence: «many people thrive at the school they did not plan for.» The words around thrive are your clues. The school is one they did not plan for, so it is a new place, and thrive must mean they do well and feel happy there.
explain: The word thrive also has a phrase. «She thrives on challenges» means she enjoys hard things and does well because of them. Others might find challenges hard, but she is happy with them. The context shows you which meaning fits.
explain: Test it: swap your meaning into the sentence. "Many people do well at the school they did not plan for" still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Thrive means to grow strong and healthy, or to do very well and be happy.
fact: «Thrive on» means to enjoy something hard and do well because of it.
fact: Plants thrive with light, water and good soil.
fact: «A thriving town» means a town that is doing well and full of life.
fact: The other forms are thrives, thrived, and thriving.
exercise: «Plants thrive with light, water and good soil.» What does thrive mean here? | Fall over and die | *Grow strong and healthy | Change colour in the autumn | Get wet in the rain
exercise: «She thrives on challenges.» What does thrives on mean? | Gets lost in a maze | Is always tired after lunch | Runs away from every hard task | *Enjoys hard things and does well because of them
exercise: Which word in «a thriving town» comes from thrive? | *thriving | town | a | full
test: «The new school helped her thrive.» What does thrive mean here? | Move house | Go back home | Stay the same | *Grow and do well
test: Ayo says a thriving business is one that is closing down. What does thriving actually mean? | Closing down | *Doing well and growing | Sleeping | Losing money slowly
exam: Read: «Many people thrive at the school they did not plan for.» What does this sentence suggest? | People get bored and leave | People must go back home | *People do well and feel happy there, even if it was not their first choice | People are always lost there
